hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22834","Bahz narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Yala ibn Ata informed me, from Abu Hammam, Abu al-Aswad said he is Abdullah ibn Yasar, from Abu Abdur-Rahman al-Fihri, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the expedition of Hunayn. We traveled on a hot day of severe heat, and we stopped under the shade of trees. When the sun declined, I put on my armor and mounted my horse, and went to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was in his tent, and I said: Peace be upon you, O Messenger of Allah, and the mercy of Allah; the time for departure has come. He said: Yes. Then he said: O Bilal. So he sprang up from under a samurah tree as though his shadow were the shadow of a bird, and said: At your service and your aid, and may I be your ransom. He said: Saddle my horse for me. So he brought out a saddle whose flaps were of palm fiber, in which there was no arrogance or haughtiness. He said: So he saddled. He said: So he mounted and we mounted, and we faced them that evening and night. The two cavalries sniffed each other, and the Muslims turned retreating as Allah, mighty and majestic, said. So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O servants of Allah, I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger. Then he said: O company of Muhajirun, I am the servant of Allah and His Messenger. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, leapt from his horse and took a handful of dust. The one who was nearest to him of those nearer than me informed me: He struck their faces with it and said: May the faces be deformed. So Allah, mighty and majestic, defeated them. Yala ibn Ata said: So their sons narrated to me from their fathers that they said: None of us remained except that his eyes and mouth were filled with dust, and we heard a rattling between heaven and earth like iron passing over an iron basin."
"22835","Affan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Yala ibn Ata informed us, from Abdullah ibn Yasar Abu Hammam, from Abu Abdur-Rahman al-Fihri, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the expedition of Hunayn. We traveled on a hot day, then he mentioned the like of it."
